{
  "case_id": "2022-21-1164",
  "document_hash": "a8499f514171198100ff438729ad112ee23cad32cf47cff98d713e6f9667cb3e",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey W. McCoy",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1164",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8499f514171198100ff438729ad112ee23cad32cf47cff98d713e6f9667cb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8499f514171-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. McCOY: Mr. Chief Justice, and may it please the Court:\nThis Court has repeatedly held that when Congress wants to make a time bar jurisdictional it must clearly state so. In passing the Quiet Title Act, Congress did not clearly state that the statute of limitations is jurisdictional. Instead, the text, context, structure, and history indicate that Congress intended the statute of limitations to be a non-jurisdictional affirmative defense."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Thomas",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1164",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8499f514171198100ff438729ad112ee23cad32cf47cff98d713e6f9667cb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8499f514171-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE THOMAS: Mr. McCoy, going beyond the text just for a bit, what do you do with the fact that this statute of limitation occurs in the context of a waiver of sovereign immunity?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey W. McCoy",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1164",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8499f514171198100ff438729ad112ee23cad32cf47cff98d713e6f9667cb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8499f514171-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. McCOY: Well, it -- mandatory, yes, Your Honor, but mandatory is different than jurisdictional. And Boechler is a -- Boechler was a waiver of sovereign immunity. This Court -- the -- this Court found that the time bar was non-jurisdictional. It even found there was equitable tolling in that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Jeffrey W. McCoy",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1164",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8499f514171198100ff438729ad112ee23cad32cf47cff98d713e6f9667cb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8499f514171-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "BUT, BEYOND THAT, WHETHER OR NOT THIS IS JURISDICTION -- IF IT'S JURISDICTIONAL, THE PLAINTIFFS HAVE THE BURDEN OF PROVING JURISDICTION, WHILE, IF IT IS A NON-JURISDICTIONAL AFFIRMATIVE DEFENSE, THEN THE GOVERNMENT WOULD HAVE THE BURDEN OF PROVING AND IT --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1164",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8499f514171198100ff438729ad112ee23cad32cf47cff98d713e6f9667cb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8499f514171-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Counsel, a Quiet Title action is tried by a judge, correct?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1164",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8499f514171198100ff438729ad112ee23cad32cf47cff98d713e6f9667cb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8499f514171-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Mr. McCoy, was there a time when this Court regarded sovereign immunity as tied to subject matter jurisdiction?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1164",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8499f514171198100ff438729ad112ee23cad32cf47cff98d713e6f9667cb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8499f514171-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: I'll ask a question then."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1164",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8499f514171198100ff438729ad112ee23cad32cf47cff98d713e6f9667cb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8499f514171-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The holding was that the Quiet Title Act's statute of limitations applies to states. That was not the holding."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Benjamin W. Snyder",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1164",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8499f514171198100ff438729ad112ee23cad32cf47cff98d713e6f9667cb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8499f514171-0001-0003",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 29,
        "start": 29
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF BENJAMIN W. SNYDER ON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENT"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Snyder",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1164",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8499f514171198100ff438729ad112ee23cad32cf47cff98d713e6f9667cb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8499f514171-0001-0005",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "bar's jurisdictional status would cause unnecessary disruption. At a broad level, it would leave the lower courts confused about when they have to comply with this Court's applications of governing law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1164",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8499f514171198100ff438729ad112ee23cad32cf47cff98d713e6f9667cb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8499f514171-0001-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I have taken Petitioners to argue that they are not asking this Court to overrule any prior decisions, that they are just asking this Court to construe Block and Mottaz narrowly to not actually mean jurisdiction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1164",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8499f514171198100ff438729ad112ee23cad32cf47cff98d713e6f9667cb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8499f514171-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Do you think that the test for determining what we held in a prior case and therefore what is protected by stare decisis is different in this context, that special clarity is required here, or is it the same test that we use in other contexts?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Amicus",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1164",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8499f514171198100ff438729ad112ee23cad32cf47cff98d713e6f9667cb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8499f514171-0002-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 55,
        "start": 55
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "My understanding of the amicus's argument was not that it would preclude settlements but that it would force parties to sort of bring these things up earlier because the government couldn't agree to a tolling arrangement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1164",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8499f514171198100ff438729ad112ee23cad32cf47cff98d713e6f9667cb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8499f514171-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 65,
        "start": 65
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: That's not the question, Mr. Snyder. The question is, why was all of that opinion necessary?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1164",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "a8499f514171198100ff438729ad112ee23cad32cf47cff98d713e6f9667cb3e",
      "evidence_id": "ev-a8499f514171-0003-0004",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 72,
        "start": 72
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "(Whereupon, at 11:09 a.m., the case was submitted.)"
    },
